cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these materials, please cite the work as below."
title: "Real Hourly Wages in the United States, 1982-2026: Replication Package"
abstract: >-
  Replication materials for an Economic Innovation Group analysis of U.S. real hourly
  wages from 1982 through 2026 across the wage distribution, age groups, generations,
  labor-market-entry cohorts, education, and sex, using Current Population Survey
  outgoing rotation group microdata from IPUMS-CPS, deflated with the PCE price index.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Glasner"
    given-names: "Benjamin"
    affiliation: "Economic Innovation Group"
year: 2026
license: MIT
keywords:
  - real wages
  - wage inequality
  - Current Population Survey
  - IPUMS
  - minimum wage
url: "https://github.com/EIG-Research/EIG-Wage-Figure-Explain-Everything-replication"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EIG-Research/EIG-Wage-Figure-Explain-Everything-replication"
